{"kind":"finding","id":"F-ledger-career-036-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/ScienceSpendingOrderingTests.cs","line":166,"method":"SortActions_AtEqualUT_PlacesEarningBeforeSpending","category":"T2","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GameActions/RecalculationEngine.cs:282; dropping the ThenBy(IsEarningType) sort key -> this cell and RecalculationEngineTests.SortActions_EarningsBeforeSpendings both red","what_it_asserts":"SortActions places an earning before a spending at an equal UT even when the spending is listed first.","why_weak":"Behavior and assertions are identical to the pre-existing twin RecalculationEngineTests.SortActions_EarningsBeforeSpendings (spend listed first, same two ordering assertions); only the literal UT and subject id differ, so the sort-key regression is already caught twice.","proposed_action":"Drop this pure sort cell (the integration cell Spending_AtSameUTAsTheEarning_IsAffordable_ViaTheTiebreak right below still pins the tiebreak end-to-end), or retarget it to a sort facet the twin does not cover, e.g. the Sequence tertiary key under one UT.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
